WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.186 --> 00:00:12.426
Ricky said one day.

2
00:00:12.446 --> 00:00:17.009
"When I grow up, I want to be an Arctic explorer."

3
00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:22.031
"Really?" said Dad.

4
00:00:22.051 --> 00:00:26.194
"Why?" "The Arctic is so cool!"

5
00:00:26.734 --> 00:00:27.474
said Ricky.

6
00:00:27.494 --> 00:00:30.016
"We learned about it in class.

7
00:00:31.808 --> 00:00:35.389
I want to see polar bears and Arctic foxes."

8
00:00:35.409 --> 00:00:39.330
"That's great," said Dad.

9
00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:41.251
"But can you live there?"

10
00:00:43.451 --> 00:00:45.352
Ricky thought about it for a while.

11
00:00:45.372 --> 00:00:49.073
"Is living in the Arctic very hard?"

12
00:00:49.613 --> 00:00:50.173
he asked.

13
00:00:51.153 --> 00:00:52.794
"Yes," said Dad.

14
00:00:52.814 --> 00:00:55.654
"Did you know it's always light during summer?"

15
00:00:57.375 --> 00:00:58.995
"No," said Ricky.

16
00:00:59.015 --> 00:01:01.356
"But that would be awesome!"

17
00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:05.943
"And it's always dark during winter," said Dad.

18
00:01:05.963 --> 00:01:08.905
"Oh," said Ricky.

19
00:01:08.925 --> 00:01:11.447
"That's not so awesome."

20
00:01:11.467 --> 00:01:15.530
"It gets very cold in the Arctic," Dad continued.

21
00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:19.112
"Hot water can turn to ice right away!"

22
00:01:19.132 --> 00:01:22.675
Ricky hugged himself and shivered.

23
00:01:22.695 --> 00:01:26.598
"So you see, son," said Dad.

24
00:01:26.618 --> 00:01:29.380
"It is not easy to live in the Arctic."

25
00:01:31.372 --> 00:01:34.154
"I think I can do it," said Ricky.

26
00:01:34.174 --> 00:01:37.756
"But I need to start training right away.

27
00:01:38.536 --> 00:01:39.857
And I'll need your help."

28
00:01:39.877 --> 00:01:42.419
"All right.

29
00:01:43.159 --> 00:01:43.859
What can I do?"

30
00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:45.120
asked Dad.

31
00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:49.883
"Can you add five dollars to my weekly allowance?"

32
00:01:50.263 --> 00:01:51.044
asked Ricky.

33
00:01:51.064 --> 00:01:53.465
"How will that help?"

34
00:01:53.985 --> 00:01:54.726
asked Dad.

35
00:01:54.746 --> 00:01:57.868
"Well," said Ricky.

36
00:01:59.437 --> 00:02:01.481
"I can buy ice cream with the money.

37
00:02:03.165 --> 00:02:05.971
That will help me get used to the cold!"
